/* Resize handles (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Resize handles"). The runtime
   registers nui-resize: a drag on it sets the size of the element its
   target names, in dp, so the size follows a scale change, and sends
   resized (ev.width, ev.height, in dp) once at the drag's end. No Python
   runs during the drag.

   <nui-resize class="nui-resize--top" edge="top" target="chat-history" min-height="25"
   	data-attr-height="history_height" data-event-resized="resized(ev.height)"/>
   	edge="top" grows the target upward from its bottom edge;
   	edge="bottom-right" grows its width and height with the drag.

   A handle needs pointer events in a document that has none (an overlay,
   the chat's body): give it nui-interactive. The host shows no resize
   cursor over it. */

nui-resize
{
	display: block;
	drag: drag;
}
.nui-resize--top
{
	height: 8dp;
}
.nui-resize--bottom-right
{
	width: 16dp;
	height: 16dp;
}
